==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|sheet-anchor}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|shoot}} <!--not sheet; see Chambers 1908 entry--> and {{m|en|anchor}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-sheet anchor.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[large]], [[spare]] [[anchor]] used in an [[emergency]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1661|author=anonymous|title=A Narrative of the Success of the Voyage of the Right Honourable {{w|Heneage Finch, 3rd Earl of Winchilsea|Heaneage Finch}}|location=London|page=3|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A52655.0001.001
|passage=The Ship having thus depth of water again, and come into a place of some convenient anchourage, our first anchour not holding us, we let fall our '''sheet anchour''' {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1719|author={{w|Daniel Defoe}}|title={{w|Robinson Crusoe}}|location=London|publisher=W. Taylor|page=10|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/004845034.0001.000
|passage=By Noon the Sea went very high indeed, and our Ship rid ''Forecastle in,'' [[ship#Verb|shipp’d]] several Seas, and we thought once or twice our Anchor had come home; upon which our Master order’d out the '''Sheet Anchor'''; so that we rode with two Anchors a-Head, and the Cables vered out to the better End.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A source of [[help]] in times of [[danger]]; [[last resort]].
#* '''1691''', {{w|Ezekiel Hopkins}}, ''An Exposition of the Ten Commandments, with Other Sermons,'' London: Nathanael Ranew, “The Ninth Commandment,” p.{{nbsp}}62,<sup>[http://name.umdl.umich.edu/B24299.0001.001]</sup>
#*: And doubtless when other Arguments have been baffled by a Temptation, this hath been a '''Sheet Anchor''' to the Soul, and hath often held it in the greatest Storms, when the Wind and Waves have beat most furiously against it.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1762|author={{w|Tobias Smollett}}|title={{w|The Life and Adventures of Sir Launcelot Greaves}}|location=London|publisher=J. Coote|volume=2|chapter=18|page=124|url=https://archive.org/details/bim_eighteenth-century_the-adventures-of-sir-la_smollett-tobias-george_1762_2/page/124/mode/1up?q=%22sheet-an%22
|passage=“{{...}} If you are afeard of goblins, brother, put your trust in the Lord, and he’ll prove a '''sheet-anchor''' to you.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1872|author={{w|Mark Twain}}|title={{w|Roughing It}}|location=Hartford, CT|publisher=American Publishing Company|chapter=14|page=115|url=https://archive.org/details/GR_762/page/115/mode/1up?q=%22sheet+anchor%22
|passage={{...}} you can imagine how like being struck by lightning it was to find myself in a country where ''written contracts were worthless!''—that main security, that '''sheet-anchor''', that absolute necessity, of business.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1955|translators=Patrick Bowles; {{w|Samuel Beckett}}|title={{w|Molloy (novel)|Molloy}}|author=Samuel Beckett|location=New York|publisher=Grove Press|section=Part 2, pp. 171-172|url=https://archive.org/details/molloynovel0000beck/page/171/mode/1up?q=%22sheet+anchors%22
|passage={{...}} I had the joyful vision of myself far from home, from the familiar faces, from all my '''sheet-anchors''', sitting on a milestone in the dark {{...}}}}
#* '''1971''', {{w|Nelson Mandela}}, letter to the wife of fellow-prisoner {{w|Mac Maharaj}} dated 1{{nbsp}}February, 1971, in Sahm Venter (ed.), ''The Prison Letters of Nelson Mandela,'' New York: Liveright, 2018,
#*: It is the prettiest portrait of her that I’ve seen. Its message is clear & unambiguous: Darling I’m the centre of the universe; '''sheet anchor''' of all your dreams!
# {{lb|en|cricket}} A [[batsman]] who provides [[dependable]] [[defence]] while a series of other batsmen [[score]] [[rapidly]].

